  "question": {
    "text": "A particle at the end of a spring executes simple harmonic motion with a period <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></math>, while the corresponding period for another spring is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math>. If the period of oscillation with the two springs in series is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>T</mi></math>, then -"
